From c7b7209791c649e0fc1c1a7985d38f37b98471a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luis Choque <luis.choque.castro@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 14:07:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(downloads): redirect to R2 instead of proxying file
 bytes

The download routes fetched every file from R2 into memory and sent it
back as a blob. They now record the download and answer 302 to the
public R2 object:

- Location: R2_PUBLIC_BASE_URL (fallback FILE_DOWNLOAD_ENDPOINT) + the
  object key encoded per path segment (spaces -> %20, never "+").
- Cache-Control: no-store, private; X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow.
- ModDownload stores the real client IP (?ip=, then CF-Connecting-IP,
  then the first X-Forwarded-For hop) and user agent, never the string
  "undefined". Mod.downloads is incremented in the same transaction.
  Only GET counts: HEAD and Range requests resuming past byte 0 are
  redirected without being counted. A failed insert never blocks the
  download.
- Unknown version: 404 (unchanged envelope).
- Stored URL outside the R2 domain (retired file server): 410 Gone.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
